the Keep. She was deliverin' classified info but got captured by goblins. I figured I'd never see her again, but Thormir stepped up. He announced he'd be comin' here to break the prisoners free. Told us he understood if no one wanted to join him. This is a fool's quest; however, there's no dwarf tougher than Thormir, so against better judgment, here I am. I want to save my friend and learn from the best. If the rest of us had one pinch o' Thormir's strength, the Rallosian scum would be runnin' home scared.'\nYou say, 'Goblins eat people?'\nGunder Ironheart says, 'O' course they do! The one we've got strung up in the cage o'er there licks his lips every time he looks at me. I'll level with ye: I don't want Thormir to see me quakin' in my boots. Could ye help put my mind at ease? Maybe ye could kill some of the [worgs] 'n' [leopards] 'n' [spiders] around the area? It'd really tickle my beard if ye could [kill all three].'\nYou say, 'I can kill leopards.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Spotting Leopard Spots'.\nGunder Ironheart says, 'The leopards don't prowl too close to here, but ye can never be too careful right? They roam mostly near a lake, huntin' the deer and fish that live 'round there.'\n\n---\n\nA dangerous plan to infiltrate Ankexfen Keep is brewing between Thormir Helmsband and his companion, Gunder Ironheart. Unfortunately, goblins aren't the only creatures the two dwarves need to watch out for. Gunder has noticed large populations of worgs, leopards, and spiders in the area. He's concerned that these wild beasts might put a stop to thormir and him before they reach the keep's walls. Gunder is doing his bet to put on a brave face for Thormir, so he discreetly asks if you'd kill some of the wildlife and help put his mind at ease before the big mission.\nKill 8 leopards.\n1\\. Clear the area of 8 leopards. 0/8 Ankexfen Keep\nYou can find some leopards on the east side of the valley, south of the goblin fort. They are also found in the northeast side of the zone, west of the goblin temple.\n\n---\n\nNote: Saying 'kill all three' assigns all 3 of Gunder's tasks at once, additional text said after accepting:\nGunder Ironheart says, 'Yer a gem among stones, aren't ye? I won't soon forget this kindness, friend.'\nYour task 'Spotting Leopard Spots' has been updated.\nYou have successfully rid the area of a leap of leopards.\nYou receive 7 copper .\nYou receive 6 silver .\nYou receive 6 gold .\nYou receive 141 platinum .\nYou have gained an ability point!\nYou gain party experience!\nYou receive 54 platinum, 1 gold and 8 silver as your split.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n141 platinum, 6 gold, 6 silver and 7 copper\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
